## Story Description
Create src/recommendations/savings_rates.py containing a SavingsRates class. Constructor takes optional yaml_path argument (default: Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent / 'data' / 'reference' / 'savings_rates.yaml'). Loads and caches the YAML in __init__. Method get(lever_type: str, category_l1: str | None = None) -> dict returns {'saving_pct': float | None, 'addressability_pct': float}. Lookup order: (1) data['categories'][category_l1][lever_type] if both keys exist, (2) data['defaults'][lever_type], (3) hardcoded fallback {'saving_pct': None, 'addressability_pct': 0.70}. Include module-level lazy singleton: _default_rates = None and get_default_rates() -> SavingsRates function.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Create file: src/recommendations/savings_rates.py
- Run: python3 -m py_compile src/recommendations/savings_rates.py — succeeds
- Verify: python3 -c "from src.recommendations.savings_rates import SavingsRates; r=SavingsRates(); v=r.get('SUPPLIER_CONSOLIDATION','Information Technology'); assert v['saving_pct']==0.12, v" — passes (IT override)
- Verify: python3 -c "from src.recommendations.savings_rates import SavingsRates; r=SavingsRates(); v=r.get('SUPPLIER_CONSOLIDATION','Unknown Category'); assert v['saving_pct']==0.08, v" — passes (default fallback)
- Verify: python3 -c "from src.recommendations.savings_rates import SavingsRates; r=SavingsRates(); v=r.get('PAYMENT_TERM_EXTENSION'); assert v['saving_pct'] is None and v['addressability_pct']==0.80, v" — passes

